      "side": 1,
      "message": "Something must be different in the g3 build, since it works fine in Dawn. We already set up the operators for this to be used as a bitmask:\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/Error.h;l\u003d283;drc\u003de08e8c85cbaa594c61e0235319dcc08b1ed3560e\nwhich is included by `ErrorSink.h`. And evidently it works fine here:\nhttps://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/Device.cpp;l\u003d705;drc\u003d84eb8ce380d0f44f4ec366398828cb4a595553e3\n\nMaybe the issue is that `Error.h` doesn\u0027t include `dawn/native/EnumClassBitmasks.h` or `webgpu/webgpu_enum_class_bitmasks.h`? (Most files get the latter via `webgpu_cpp.h`.) But I\u0027m surprised if the template overload compiles at all if the base template isn\u0027t in scope at all.",
      "parentUuid": "a1135c7a_c509e3fa",
